{"key":"enterprise/T1207","id":"T1207","name":"Rogue Domain Controller","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["defense-impairment"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may register a rogue Domain Controller to enable manipulation of Active Directory data. DCShadow may be used to create a rogue Domain Controller (DC). DCShadow is a method of manipulating Active Directory (AD) data, including objects and schemas, by registering (or reusing an inactive registration) and simulating the behavior of a DC. Once registered, a rogue DC may be able to inject and replicate changes into AD infrastructure for…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1207","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--564998d8-ab3e-4123-93fb-eccaa6b9714a","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.634Z","source_object_version":"3.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0084","name":"Active Directory Credential Request","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0084","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--02d090b6-8157-48da-98a2-517f7edd49fc","page":"telemetry/DC0084/"},{"id":"DC0071","name":"Active Directory Object Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0071","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--5c6de881-bc70-4070-855a-7a9631a407f7","page":"telemetry/DC0071/"},{"id":"DC0087","name":"Active Directory Object Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0087","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--18b236d8-7224-488f-9d2f-50076a0f653a","page":"telemetry/DC0087/"},{"id":"DC0066","name":"Active Directory Object Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0066","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--5b8b466b-2c81-4fe7-946f-d677a74ae3db","page":"telemetry/DC0066/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-compo